.TH EVENTWHY 1
.SH NAME
eventwhy \- summarize bounded Docker event evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eventwhy
[--input EVENTS.ndjson] [--max-events 2000]
.PP
.B eventwhy
--collect --context NAME [--window 5m] [--timeout 20s]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Groups container events by resource, action, and reported exit code. Preserves
counts and first/last timestamps. Drops unrelated labels and payloads. Exit 137
does not by itself establish an out-of-memory cause.
.PP
Live collection retrieves a finite historical window. Docker history is limited,
so completeness of that window remains unknown and the result is partial.
This command does not provide a continuous monitor or current health verdict.
.SH OPTIONS
Use --help for all bounds and flags. Input is limited to 4 MiB and each record to
256 KiB. Exceeding input or record limits produces partial evidence.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 supplied evidence parsed; 2 invalid usage; 3 partial evidence; 4 input/output failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
rcdo watch, docs/accessible-operations/DEMO.md
